# Working Principles

## Simplicity
- Build the simplest thing that works for the current request. No speculative features, options, extension points or
  "for later" code. Abstractions (interfaces, base classes, generics) only when there are two real users or a test needs the seam.
- Do not create files you do not need: no new docs/READMEs unless asked, no empty folders, no one-line wrapper classes,
  no new projects. Prefer adding to the existing file for that feature.
- Delete what becomes unused in the same change (code, components, resource keys, packages). Git history keeps it.
- Keep changes scoped to the request; mention unrelated issues you notice instead of fixing them silently.

## Reuse existing patterns
- Before writing something new, find the closest existing example and copy its shape:
  - CRUD feature: the users module (`UsersController` + `UserService` + `UserRepository` + `User : SoftDeletableEntity` +
    Contracts requests with ErrorCodes + `UsersApi` + `UsersViewModel` + `UserFormViewModel`/`UserFormView` + tests on both sides).
    Step by step: the `new-feature` skill (`.cursor/skills/new-feature/SKILL.md`)
  - log-style endpoint: `ActivityLogsController` + `ActivityLogService` + repository + Contracts DTOs + integration tests
  - list page: `NumberedListViewModel` (or `PagedListViewModel` for logs) subclass + `DataTable` view + `AppRoutes` entry + desktop tests
  - UI: components from `Docs/shared-components.md` before writing new XAML
- One way per concern: `ApiClient` for HTTP, `IActivityLogger` for activity, `ISystemErrorLogger`/`ErrorReporter` for errors,
  `PerformanceMonitor` for speed debugging (overlay + perf log; do not sprinkle stopwatches in view models),
  `DialogService`/`ToastService` for feedback, `FormViewModel` + `ShowFormAsync` for forms, DataAnnotations with `ErrorCodes`
  + `AppException` for validation and expected errors, `TimeProvider` for the current time, `INumberSequence` for readable
  numbers, `ClinicContext` for clinic details and currency, `PrintService` + `ClinicPage` for printouts,
  `ConnectionMonitor` for server reachability. Do not add a second mechanism.

## Dependencies
- No new NuGet package, project or external tool without asking the user first (say what it replaces and why the
  existing stack cannot do it). Packages go in the lowest layer that needs them; EF Core/Npgsql only in Infrastructure.
- Package versions live only in `Directory.Packages.props` (a `.csproj` `PackageReference` has no `Version`); settings
 shared by all projects live in `Directory.Build.props`. Warnings are errors: fix the cause, and only switch a rule off
 in `.editorconfig` with a one-line reason when it does not fit the project.
- Keep the SQLite fallback possible (see `project-architecture.mdc`).

## Layers are never bypassed
- Controller -> Application service -> repository interface -> Infrastructure. Controllers never touch `AppDbContext` or
  repositories (only exception: `HealthController`'s connectivity check); Application never references EF Core; Domain references nothing.
- Desktop -> `Services/Api` -> HTTP -> API. The desktop never references backend projects, the database or Infrastructure.
- Views -> view models -> services. Views hold no logic beyond view-only code-behind; view models never create views or windows directly
  (use `NavigationService`, `DialogService`).
- Do not "temporarily" break a rule to make something work; if a rule blocks the task, stop and ask.

## Ask before
- Changing architecture: layers, project structure, dependency direction, auth model, navigation/shell design,
  database provider or schema conventions, the logging engines.
- Adding business modules or business logic the user did not request.
- Renaming/moving many files, changing public API routes or Contracts that the other side already uses.
- Anything destructive: dropping data, rewriting migrations that already exist, deleting docs.

## Definition of done
- Builds with no new warnings; tests added per `testing.mdc` and passing (`./scripts/test.ps1`).
- New user-visible strings in both `Strings.resx` and `Strings.ar.resx`; layout changes covered by headless view tests
 (Arabic/RTL and narrow widths where the layout depends on them).
- Verify with the build and `./scripts/test.ps1` only. Do not start the app, take screenshots, render frames or run
 end-to-end/visual simulations unless the user asks for it.
- Docs/rules updated in the same change when a pattern, component or command changes.
